      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19402",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/23/23f075900fd3cc3092cb2c0bfc3cfc09f0bedbd077eebc1a6419ed191fef0f3b.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curve $y =-\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis for $-1 \\le x \\le 0$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are semicircles, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
