      ":question/problem": "![](images/76/76afce4c1a5fbf0c1547621141c03d3fba3d748eab4adae9dde33d403b313040.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the line $y = \\frac{x}{2} + 1$ and the $x$-axis for $-2 \\le x \\le 1$, as shown above. If cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are quarter-circles, which of the following gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
